  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "The velocity vector $v=\u27e8u,v\u27e9,$ measured in $\\text{m}/\\text{s},$ of a particle $P$ at time $t$ seconds is given by\n\n$$\nv=\u27e8{t}^{2}+2t,6{t}^{2}-3\u27e9.\n$$\n\nFind the magnitude of the acceleration of $P$ at time $t=0.$",
  "worked_solution": "To compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}+2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6{t}^{2}-3)\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e82t+2,\\,12t\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the acceleration at time $t=0,$ we substitute $t=0$ into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(0) & =\u27e82(0)+2,12(0)\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e82,0\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the magnitude of the acceleration, we compute $|a(0)|:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|a(0)| & =|\u27e82,0\u27e9| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2)^{2}+(0)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
